\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Comparison of cell cycle dynamics between experimental data and the null model. (a) Cell volume vs. time for the experimental data of {\it  E. coli} in the glucose+12 a.a. medium in Ref. \cite  {Taheri2015cell}, where the cell volume is normalized by the average birth volume $\bar  V_b$. (b) The same as (a) but for the simulation data. Here, $a=0.026$, $b=0.037$, with the time unit 1 min. (c-d) Experimental distributions of the normalized doubling time $T/\overline  {T}$ (c) and normalized added volume throughout one cell cycle $\Delta V/\overline  {\Delta V}$ (d). (e-f) The corresponding distributions generated by the null model simulation.}}{2}{}}
